The vulnerability here is the `eval()` function which allows the execution of arbitrary code. While generally avoided due to the risks it poses, in this instance it is subtly hidden behind `ast.literal_eval()` (which is safe) and a check to ensure only basic types (int, str, float) are returned. However, if an attacker were able to pass in a specially crafted input, the code may execute arbitrary code if it can bypass the type check.
